# Integration — exact address repair

Date: 2026-10-31. Author: Grok-2. This page names the next seam after the 05.02 repair. It does not change `app/`, `prime_cycle.py`, `prime_review.py`, or the placement lab.

## What this lab now checks

`labs/review-construction-pass01/construct.py` still renders through pinned `prime_review.py report`. The target path must equal the destination derived from the source page, pass, and kind. An N5NN member must be `{N}1{NN}.{subject}`, and the typed origin `book`, `page`, and `batch` must name that source. The hashed binding is `review-task-binding/2`. It includes source book, page, and pass, and the declared assignment path, beside the task, evidence, agreement, and receipt byte identities. The target file hash stays the write token. `review-task-binding/1` is not emitted and is not upgraded. Custody stays `not-established`. No member is allocated.

A coherent nonzero N7NN page can render on its own review tail. A coherent nonzero N5NN page can be bound. Preview and apply of that record stop at the pinned capture member pattern `^01[0-9]{2}\.[a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*$`, which refuses `1199.{subject}` with `bad member` and writes nothing. This pack leaves that pin unchanged.

## Future cycle change

`labs/prime-cycle-pass01/prime_cycle.py` still compares `source.page_sha256`. A review written onto that page changes the page hash, so a later `record` refuses with `source changed since read: source`. This lab does not patch that function.

The smallest cycle change is one new accepted binding input, `review-task-binding/2`, beside the existing page hash. Staleness for the judgment uses that binding, including the normalized source and the assignment path. The page hash remains the compare-and-swap token for the write. A rendered review that leaves source identity, assignment path and bytes, evidence, receipt, and agreement unchanged must not be reported as source-stale. A change to any of those must. A stored `review-task-binding/1` preimage is a different object. It stays readable as history and is not treated as this binding. `closes_work`, `releases_action`, and `authenticates_actor` stay false.

Do not add a second status engine. One integration worker should own the shared facade change. No parallel edit to `app/librarian.py`.

## Future app entry

A later pack can add one command, `prime-review-construct`, with declaration `app/prime-review.json` pointing at `labs/review-construction-pass01/construct.py`. The command passes through stdout, stderr, and the integer exit. It refuses a fixture root inside the checkout, a drifted pin, and a linked path. It does not gain `draft`, reserve, or capture.

## Pinned member pattern

Rendering `{N}1{NN}.{subject}` for a leading digit other than `0` needs the pinned `prime_review.py` member pattern to accept that line. That is an edit to an existing module. It is outside this pack. Until that pin changes, nonzero N5NN construction stops at the report tool after this lab's own address checks have passed.

## Adapter after reviewed placement

The receipt object remains the seam. A later adapter, written only after Prime reviews the 0521 migration, fills that object from the placed bytes. For this source the matching line is `0122.review-construction`. The adapter reads the placed receipt, return bytes, and manifest, and sets `placement` to `n5nn-matching-line`. It does not scan the old `01NN` table and it does not allocate. N7NN keeps `page_local` `05.NN.return.md` and `member` null. `labs/return-placement-pass01` was not imported here. Until that adapter exists, a caller passes the three files explicitly. A boolean does not authenticate them. No new Director decision is required to describe that later fill.

## Minimal next test

One disposable N5NN page in workflow space `0`, with a `PENDING.` review section. Apply this constructor. In a second process, run the updated cycle read and record using `review-task-binding/2` computed before the render. The record must succeed, and the stored binding must equal the pre-render binding. Then change one evidence byte, and show the new record refused. Separately, a `1599` fixture must show this lab's derived member `1199.{subject}` and the current pin refusal, until the pin itself is widened. Do not point that test at the live work book, and do not run inventory, bridge fixtures, or race probes. AR-01 stays held.

## Not in this pack

No universal face builder. No worker launch. No claim that the live cycle is already fixed. No Git publication.
